# Long-lived cache headers for static, content-hashed-by-path assets.
# GitHub Pages does not read this file (fixed ~10min Cache-Control, no
# per-file override available) — this only takes effect if the site is
# ever served from a host that honors _headers, e.g. Netlify or
# Cloudflare Pages. Flagged by PageSpeed as "Use efficient cache
# lifetimes" (~1MB opportunity); this is the fix for that host class.
# On GitHub Pages, the real fix is fronting the domain with Cloudflare
# and setting a Cache Rule / Edge TTL for /public assets.

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
